<article class="env-corollary" id="04HK">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/04HK">Corollary <span data-tag="04HK">11.5.0.74</span>.</a> See Remark <a data-tag="04HJ" href="/tag/04HJ">3.5.1.19</a>. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
<p>
<strong>Proof.</strong>
      Using Proposition <a data-tag="00UV" href="/tag/00UV">3.1.8.1</a>, we can choose a commutative diagram 
    <p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix@R =50pt@C=50pt{ X \ar [r] \ar [d]^{f} &amp;  X' \ar [d]^{f'} \\ Y \ar [r] &amp;  Y' } \]
</div>
<p>
       where the horizontal maps are inner anodyne, $Y'$ is a Kan complex, and $f'$ is a Kan fibration. Then $f$ is $n$-connective if and only if $f'$ is $n$-connective, and $f$ is a weak homotopy equivalence if and only if $f'$ is a homotopy equivalence (Proposition <a data-tag="00UB" href="/tag/00UB">3.1.7.13</a>). The desired result now follows by applying Proposition <a data-tag="00X1" href="/tag/00X1">3.2.7.2</a> to the Kan fibration $f'$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
</p>
</p></p></article>
